    typography: "Cinzel Regular governs the lyric band — display-weight roman capitals that carry the weight of stone inscription without becoming decorative. Size: 72px at 1080p (scales proportionally at 4K), tracked at +80 (em units: 0.08em), set in ALL CAPS, centred on the φ spine. Word-by-word reveal: each word fades in at 180 ms opacity ease-in, held, with the next word arriving precisely on the 4–5 s line interval — no animation beyond opacity; the words arrive as a plainchant syllable arrives, one at a time, placed. Active word: #FFF2D6 at full opacity. Preceding words on the same line: #FFF2D6 at 55% opacity — they are the already-sung phrase, present but subordinate. Line transition: outgoing line fades to 0 over 400 ms as incoming line begins its first word, so there is always a single moment of silence between lines. Scripture reference (when present): Noto Serif Italic, 28px, #E89B5A, set bel",
    imageLogic: "The concept plate (/sanctuary-plates/calm-galilee-dawn.jpg) is composited via globalCompositeOperation 'luminosity' at plateBlend (operator-adjustable 0.18–0.38 default 0.26), drawn fullscreen behind all procedural layers. It does not decorate the scene — it governs it: a one-time 24×14 luminance sample is taken from the plate on init and stored as the cantus firmus grid. Every bokeh mote, every hill silhouette vertex, every caustic-ring seed point must trace its position to a grid cell with luminance above threshold (0.35). The plate is never shown at full opacity; it is always subordinate to the procedural scene, functioning as the structural undervoice — heard but not seen, the way a cantus firmus is felt in a motet without being the melody the ear follows.",
    texture: "The optical pass is keyed to the Classical lens: simulated 35mm Kodak Ektar grain (generated noise field, octave 1, amplitude 0.018, scaled to frame), applied as a luminance-only overlay — texture without colour contamination. A single anamorphic lens flare blooms along the φ spine from the sun position: two horizontal streak lines at 1px and 0.4px, #E89B5A at 35% and 18% opacity, length proportional to swell amplitude. No light leaks that cross the text-safe band. The water surface is a layered gradient from #131829 (deep) through #3E334E (mid) to a narrow band of #E89B5A at the horizon reflection — three gradient stops, no more, because a water surface in stillness has hierarchy not chaos. Film grain and the anamorphic streak are the only optical-pass elements; the Classical lens does not permit the colour-punch pass to shift the palette — colour is fixed to the four declared values.",
