    direction: "A vertical golden-ratio spine at φ=0.618 divides the canvas; the horizon sits at the lower third (y=0.333), giving sky two-thirds and water one-third — water is the active plane, sky is the breathing silence above it. The concept plate is sampled once at init into a 24×14 luminance grid (cantus firmus); every hill bezier vertex, every caustic-ring origin, and every bokeh-mote position is authorised only by a grid cell above luma 0.32 — the plate is consulted before anything is placed, not credited after. Three water-gradient stops (#131829 deep → #3E334E mid → #E89B5A at the horizon seam), a cached boat Path2D on the φ spine at the horizon, and concentric caustic rings in φ-ratio spacing (radii × 1.618 per successive ring) driven by the vocal envelope; swell widens the sun-path column symmetrically about the φ spine; bass translates the boat ±2.5px on y with a 4.2s period spring-damped (k=0.08, ζ=0.85). Optical pass: Kodak Ektar-style monochrome noise field (pre-baked 512×512, scrolled 0.4px/frame diagonal, amplitude 0.022) plus a single anamorphic streak 1px tall on the sun-axis at #E89B5A 30% opacity scaling with swell — no light leaks crossing the text-safe band, no linen weave,",
