    imageLogic: "The concept plate /sanctuary-plates/calm-contemporary-bokeh-leaks.jpg enters as the scene's atmospheric memory, not its background. It is blended via plateBlend at a base opacity of 0.28, multiply-blended into the procedural scene so its golden bokeh leaks reinforce — never replace — the renderer's own depth planes. The plate is scaled to cover-fill, then subjected to a slow generative drift: a 0.04px/frame vertical float (upward, looping every 420 seconds) that makes the plate feel like smoke rising, never like a still. During a Swell event the plate's blendOpacity rises from 0.28 to 0.44 over 1.2 seconds (spring-damped, k=0.12), pulling the concept plate's warm leak colour into the upper apse — the photograph earns its moment when the music earns it. The plate is never the hero; it is the memory of a real sanctuary that the renderer is re-dreaming.",
